--- filmcraft.orig/docs/all-dings-addons.md	2026-11-04 19:00:17.087402634 +0100
+++ filmcraft/docs/all-dings-addons.md	2026-11-04 21:17:43.790317873 +0100
@@ -60,3 +60,15 @@
 All-Dings keeps Channel graphs, RCZ decoding, canonical measurement time and
 PNG decoding in its adapter. FilmCraft only sees its ordinary media interface;
 its project schema, timeline and compositor are unchanged.
+
+## Program-picture source provenance
+
+`perf.stats.monitor` additionally reports `sequence`, exact `timeTicks` (string),
+and `sourceReads` (`item`, file `path`, exact `timeTicks`) for the displayed
+Program picture. Completed frame jobs retain their actual media demands,
+including source-cache hits. The trace is bounded to 256 distinct demands and
+256 pictures; an absent trace or `sourceReadsTruncated` must not be treated as a
+complete snapshot. `renderPreview` indicates a flattened preview without live
+source provenance. Cancelled and still-loading jobs never publish a trace.
+ArtCraft uses this read-only information only on explicit user request to copy
+a paused, current picture's source positions back into its Channel builder.
